## Networking

{{#if flags.usesDio}}
- Use the shared `Dio` instance from `lib/src/config/app_config.dart` — never `Dio()` inside a widget or screen.
- Prefer `DioService` under `lib/src/services/` for HTTP calls. Network logs come from `DioLoggingInterceptor` middleware — do not add `AppLogger.network` in service methods.
- Wrap calls with `runTask(operation: 'dio.get', category: LogCategory.network, ...)`.
- Map transport errors to `Failure` / `FutureEither` — do not leak raw `DioException` to UI.
{{/if}}

{{#if (and flags.usesHttp (not flags.usesDio))}}
- Use the HTTP service exported from `lib/src/services/` — do not call `http.get` directly from presentation code.
- Network logs come from `LoggingHttpClient` middleware on `AppConfig.httpClient`.
- Wrap calls with `runTask(operation: 'http.get', category: LogCategory.network, ...)`.
- Handle timeouts and socket errors explicitly in the service layer.
{{/if}}

{{#unless (or flags.usesDio flags.usesHttp)}}
- No HTTP client package is enabled — use mock/local data patterns already in the template or add Dio/HTTP via `pubspec.yaml` deliberately.
{{/unless}}
